00:58:04,799 --> 00:58:10,799
Valkyrie (German: Walküre, as featured in the opening sequence) is a 2008 historical thriller film directed
by Bryan Singer, written by Christopher McQuarrie and Nathan Alexander, starring Tom Cruise.

13
01:02:55,199 --> 01:03:01,199
The film is set in Nazi Germany during World War II and depicts the 20 July plot in 1944 by German army officers to
assassinate Adolf Hitler and to use the Operation Valkyrie national emergency plan to take control of the country.

14
01:07:45,599 --> 01:07:51,599
The film was released by American studio United Artists and stars Cruise as
Colonel Claus von Stauffenberg, one of the key plotters.

15
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
The supporting cast includes Kenneth Branagh, Bill Nighy,
Eddie Izzard, Terence Stamp, and Tom Wilkinson.

16
01:17:26,399 --> 01:17:32,399
Cruise's casting caused controversy among German politicians and members of the von Stauffenberg family
due to the actor's practice of Scientology, which is viewed with suspicion in Germany.

17
01:22:16,799 --> 01:22:22,799
Because of this, the filmmakers initially had difficulty setting up filming locations in Germany,
but they were later given access to locations such as Berlin's historic Bendlerblock.

18
01:27:07,199 --> 01:27:13,199
German newspapers and filmmakers supported the film and its intention
to spread global awareness of von Stauffenberg's plot.

19
01:31:57,599 --> 01:32:03,599
The film changed release dates several times, from as early as
June 27, 2008, to as late as February 13, 2009.

20
01:36:48,000 --> 01:36:54,000
The changing calendar and poor response to United Artists's initial marketing campaign drew criticism about the film's viability; following a positive test
screening, Valkyrie's release in North America was ultimately changed to December 25, 2008, and it opened in Germany on January 22, 2009.

21
01:41:38,399 --> 01:41:44,399
United Artists renewed its marketing campaign to reduce its focus
on Cruise and to highlight Singer's credentials.

22
01:46:28,799 --> 01:46:34,799
The film received generally positive reviews from
critics and grossed $201 million worldwide.

23
01:51:19,199 --> 01:51:25,199
The film explores themes of friendship, suicide, plan,
berlin, germany, husband wife relationship.

24
01:56:09,599 --> 01:56:15,599
The tone is emotional and intense.
